  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37143898",
      "title": "Mutating Values in Memory & Making Sense of var, final & const",
      "lectureOrder": 152,
      "videoOrder": 140,
      "sourceHash": "bf3ddcd1c706d2338979d5183a90bac478370bf9914ef2fd412fc787927fa18a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.42,
          "en": "So now we learned a lot about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.42,
          "end": 4.68,
          "en": "Flutters internals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.68,
          "end": 8.67,
          "en": "How it updates the UI and why we sometimes need keys?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.67,
          "end": 11.07,
          "en": "Now I wanna conclude this section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.07,
          "end": 13.44,
          "en": "by taking a look at a Dart concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.44,
          "end": 14.673,
          "en": "that can be confusing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.57,
          "end": 16.56,
          "en": "In this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.56,
          "end": 18.63,
          "en": "we sometimes had a case like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 18.63,
          "end": 22.14,
          "en": "where we had a list, like let's say numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.14,
          "end": 24.42,
          "en": "One, two, three",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.42,
          "end": 26.85,
          "en": "and then we called add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.85,
          "end": 29.85,
          "en": "and added a new value to this list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.85,
          "end": 32.19,
          "en": "And this can be confusing because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.19,
          "end": 34.95,
          "en": "isn't this a final list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 34.95,
          "end": 38.67,
          "en": "so why can we add new values if it's final?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.67,
          "end": 39.9,
          "en": "And that's a good question",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 39.9,
          "end": 41.31,
          "en": "and it's therefore really important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 41.31,
          "end": 43.44,
          "en": "to understand what's going on here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 43.44,
          "end": 47.28,
          "en": "Final simply means that this variable is final,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 47.28,
          "end": 50.73,
          "en": "so you can't assign a new value to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 50.73,
          "end": 54.003,
          "en": "If I would try to set numbers to a different list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.08,
          "end": 56.88,
          "en": "like this, I would get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 56.88,
          "end": 59.04,
          "en": "because this variable is final",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 59.04,
          "end": 61.74,
          "en": "and it can therefore only be set once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 61.74,
          "end": 62.85,
          "en": "So put in our words,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 62.85,
          "end": 65.37,
          "en": "I can't use this assignment operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 65.37,
          "end": 69.9,
          "en": "this equal sign again on a variable that is final.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 69.9,
          "end": 71.88,
          "en": "This does not work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 71.88,
          "end": 75.78,
          "en": "This here, however, does not assign a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 75.78,
          "end": 77.85,
          "en": "instead it use the existing value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 77.85,
          "end": 78.93,
          "en": "stored in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 78.93,
          "end": 81.21000000000001,
          "en": "So this existing list stored in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 81.21000000000001,
          "end": 83.7,
          "en": "and adds a new value to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 83.7,
          "end": 87.06,
          "en": "It does not store a new value in the variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 87.06,
          "end": 88.8,
          "en": "The value is the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 88.8,
          "end": 91.77,
          "en": "it's the same object in memory, the same list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 91.77,
          "end": 94.02000000000001,
          "en": "It's just that object in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 94.02000000000001,
          "end": 95.673,
          "en": "that's changed behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 96.50999999999999,
          "end": 99.9,
          "en": "When assigning a new value like I tried it to do here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 99.9,
          "end": 102.21000000000001,
          "en": "I'm actually creating a new list in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 102.21000000000001,
          "end": 104.82,
          "en": "A totally new object in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 104.82,
          "end": 106.8,
          "en": "I'm not editing an existing object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 106.8,
          "end": 107.91,
          "en": "I'm creating a new one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 107.91,
          "end": 111.27000000000001,
          "en": "and I can't assign this new object to numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 111.27000000000001,
          "end": 114.06,
          "en": "That is what final prevents.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 114.06,
          "end": 116.91,
          "en": "And that's what's different if I use var instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 116.91,
          "end": 117.96000000000001,
          "en": "With the var,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 117.96000000000001,
          "end": 120.69,
          "en": "I am allowed to assign a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 120.69,
          "end": 122.43,
          "en": "This is now possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 122.43,
          "end": 125.16,
          "en": "because with var we create a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 125.16,
          "end": 126.84,
          "en": "that can be reassigned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 126.84,
          "end": 128.58,
          "en": "So where you can overwrite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 128.58,
          "end": 131.94,
          "en": "the existing value with a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 131.94,
          "end": 134.49,
          "en": "You can also still edit an existing value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 134.49,
          "end": 136.62,
          "en": "but you can also override it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 136.62,
          "end": 139.65,
          "en": "That's the difference between final and var.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 139.65,
          "end": 141.63,
          "en": "And then we also have const.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 141.63,
          "end": 145.29,
          "en": "With const, you also can't assign a new value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 145.29,
          "end": 147.78,
          "en": "but here you also get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 147.78,
          "end": 150.78,
          "en": "if I open the debug console and restart the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 150.78,
          "end": 154.71,
          "en": "if you try to add it an existing value in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 154.71,
          "end": 156.93,
          "en": "Here we get an error that I can't add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 156.93,
          "end": 158.673,
          "en": "to an unmodifiable list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 159.78,
          "end": 161.34,
          "en": "And I'm getting this error here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 161.34,
          "end": 162.54,
          "en": "because with const,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 162.54,
          "end": 163.98,
          "en": "you're telling Dart that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 163.98,
          "end": 165.51,
          "en": "it's not just final,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 165.51,
          "end": 166.98,
          "en": "but this value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 166.98,
          "end": 170.79,
          "en": "also can't be manipulated behind the scenes essentially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 170.79,
          "end": 172.803,
          "en": "That's what const does here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 173.67000000000002,
          "end": 175.74,
          "en": "Now, when we used const on widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 175.74,
          "end": 178.11,
          "en": "we're essentially doing the same thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 178.11,
          "end": 181.5,
          "en": "We're saying that it can't be manipulated behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 181.5,
          "end": 184.98,
          "en": "and that's why Flutter is able to reuse those widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 184.98,
          "end": 187.77,
          "en": "if we use the same widget with the same configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 187.77,
          "end": 190.29,
          "en": "in different places of our widget tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 190.29,
          "end": 193.86,
          "en": "because it knows that it can't change in a magical place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 193.86,
          "end": 196.68,
          "en": "and it therefore can't break one part of the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 196.68,
          "end": 199.44,
          "en": "just because it changed in another part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 199.44,
          "end": 202.29,
          "en": "With const, it's clear that this can't happen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 202.29,
          "end": 205.47,
          "en": "And here we're using const in front of a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 205.47,
          "end": 208.68,
          "en": "whereas here we're using it in front of a variable name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 208.68,
          "end": 210.48,
          "en": "but we could also write this as",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 210.48,
          "end": 213.18,
          "en": "final numbers equals const like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 213.18,
          "end": 215.49,
          "en": "to make this list unmodifiable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 215.49,
          "end": 217.86,
          "en": "and make this variable unmodifiable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 217.86,
          "end": 219.75,
          "en": "But we can also use a shortcut here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 219.75,
          "end": 222.72,
          "en": "and add constant front of the variable like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 222.72,
          "end": 224.1,
          "en": "This makes the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 224.1,
          "end": 227.16,
          "en": "and the variable unmodifiable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 227.16,
          "end": 230.94,
          "en": "With final, we make just the variable unmodifiable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 230.94,
          "end": 233.403,
          "en": "and with var, everything is allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 234.32999999999998,
          "end": 237.27,
          "en": "So this difference between var, final and const",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 237.27,
          "end": 238.5,
          "en": "is really important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 238.5,
          "end": 240.78,
          "en": "and it is important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 240.78,
          "end": 242.1,
          "en": "and keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 242.1,
          "end": 246.15,
          "en": "that when you create data with var, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 246.15,
          "end": 248.343,
          "en": "this data is stored in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 249.18,
          "end": 252.33,
          "en": "So in this case, this list object is stored in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 252.33,
          "end": 254.28,
          "en": "This line of code which you see here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 254.28,
          "end": 257.52,
          "en": "creates a new list object and stores it in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 257.52,
          "end": 261.12,
          "en": "and in the end it's this address of this data in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 261.12,
          "end": 262.86,
          "en": "that's stored in the variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 262.86,
          "end": 264.843,
          "en": "That is what happens behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 266.07,
          "end": 270.54,
          "en": "Now if you override the value in the variable like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 270.54,
          "end": 272.4,
          "en": "a new object is created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 272.4,
          "end": 274.89,
          "en": "and stored in memory with a new address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 274.89,
          "end": 278.01,
          "en": "and this new address overwrites the existing address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 278.01,
          "end": 280.08,
          "en": "in the existing variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 280.08,
          "end": 281.94,
          "en": "So in the end, the data in the variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 281.94,
          "end": 283.38,
          "en": "is overwritten, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 283.38,
          "end": 285.09000000000003,
          "en": "but technically it's the address.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 285.09000000000003,
          "end": 288.753,
          "en": "Now the variable points at a different object in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 289.98,
          "end": 291.18,
          "en": "In this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 291.18,
          "end": 294.15,
          "en": "if the old list which only included max",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 294.15,
          "end": 296.15999999999997,
          "en": "was only stored in users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 296.15999999999997,
          "end": 298.08,
          "en": "and not used anywhere else in the code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 298.08,
          "end": 300,
          "en": "Dart would actually recognize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 300,
          "end": 302.31,
          "en": "that this old list isn't used anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 302.31,
          "end": 304.26,
          "en": "and would indeed remove it from memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 304.26,
          "end": 306.12,
          "en": "to free up memory again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 306.12,
          "end": 308.19,
          "en": "But Dart does this automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 308.19,
          "end": 311.55,
          "en": "This is a process called garbage collecting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 311.55,
          "end": 314.31,
          "en": "So that is what happens if you create new values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 314.31,
          "end": 316.83299999999997,
          "en": "and store these values in variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 317.67,
          "end": 318.84,
          "en": "Now for many objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 318.84,
          "end": 321.48,
          "en": "you cannot just create those objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 321.48,
          "end": 323.97,
          "en": "you can for example, not just create a list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 323.97,
          "end": 326.4,
          "en": "but you can also manipulate existing objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 326.4,
          "end": 329.46,
          "en": "For example, by calling add on a list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 329.46,
          "end": 332.22,
          "en": "And this indeed does not create a new list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 332.22,
          "end": 335.13,
          "en": "but it adds the existing list in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 335.13,
          "end": 338.46,
          "en": "The address is the same because the object is the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 338.46,
          "end": 341.97,
          "en": "It's just some internal data of that object that changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 341.97,
          "end": 345.09000000000003,
          "en": "and therefore the address and the object stays unchanged.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
